WEBVTT

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:01.810
Nothing good has ever happened
to me on a rainy day.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.880
My first day
of school...

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.550
School field trips...

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.520
Come to think of it
my first love, too...

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.510
Share an umbrella?

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.210
Thank you!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.510
I just love
rainy days!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.700
I like them, too.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:21.930
We like all
the same things!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.080
Godai?

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.170
I've come to
walk you home.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:44.890
Kyoko!

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.300
Godai!

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.610
Kyoko!!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.760
Kyoko--

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.140
Godai!

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.510
S-S-Sakamoto!

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.220
Gee, it's great to
see you! Lend me 2000.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.850
Oh, yeah, you're broke. Answer
for me at roll and we'll be even.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.680
That's the 4 o'clock linguistics
class. You're savin' my life.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.770
Wh-- Wh-- Wh--

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.480
Like I said, rainy days have
always gone this way for me.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.730
Oh, dear. If only I'd
finished shopping sooner--

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.780
Be my guest.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.940
M-Miss Nanao?

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:15.160
Yeah.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.710
This is really
nice of you.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.250
Not at all. I've got
nothing better to do.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.020
I need a topic!
A topic!

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.070
Is Godai at school?

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.480
Yes. He should be
home by nightfall.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.770
Is he usually
home so early?

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.820
Well... Nightfall on
Monday and Wednesday...

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.550
8 PM on Tuesday
and Friday...

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.690
He tutors on Thursday,
so it's about 10.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.880
I don't know
about Saturday--

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.810
You know everything!
How come?

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.550
Well, I'm
the manager--

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.570
Is that right?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.480
Of course, it is.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.620
Then you know the schedules
of all your other tenants, too?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:03.940
Why of course.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.820
Actually,
I don't, but--

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.990
You must be a
great manager!

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.100
See ya
tomorrow, Teach!

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:15.240
Bye!!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.090
Go straight
home, now.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.610
Okay!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.270
C'mon, let's go!

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.850
Soichiro! What
are you doing?

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.860
I'm so sorry!
He ruined your skirt!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.960
It's nothing, really.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.440
Come back with me. You
don't want the stain to set.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.990
You don't have to.
It's really nothing--

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.270
There. You can wear my
skirt until yours dries.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:16.280
Thanks!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.320
Her waist is tiny!

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:22.980
I'll get tea.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.360
Don't mind me.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:35.420
Here you go.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.180
Thank you!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.440
I need a topic!
A topic!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.050
Manager?

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.420
So what do you
think of Godai?

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.130
I, uhh...
What do you mean?

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.370
You always see him, right?
What kind of person is he?

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:02.570
It's hard to
put into words...

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.930
I wonder if he's
dating anyone else.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.350
You're the only one
I know of.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.550
You think so!?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:11.400
Yes.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.850
I used to go to
Clock Hill Junior High.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:20.940
Really?

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.250
That was a quick
change of subject.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:28.230
And Godai looks just like
my first love, back then.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.450
Your first love?

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.890
He probably didn't even
know that I was alive.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.790
So he was an
interesting man?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.460
He was wonderful!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.620
Wonderful, AND he
was just like Godai?

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.160
He was so manly.
So cool--

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.250
So where's the
resemblance?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.390
He was always the last one to
leave the cafeteria at lunch.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:55.840
I don't
understand this.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.960
You sure have
a handsome boyfriend.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.750
Remember? That
day we first met.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.210
Coach Mitaka? He and
I are just friends.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:07.800
No way!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.700
It's true.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:13.750
So you don't
have a boyfriend?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:21.710
I'm--

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.270
Y-You're a widow?

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.170
I'm sorry...
Me and my big mouth, huh?

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.120
It's all right.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.310
Although, it does
bring back memories.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.220
He was also
my first love.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.470
Go on ahead.
I have to do something.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.550
What is it?

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:51.550
Bye-bye.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:52.700
Kyoko!

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.760
Where Mr. Otonashi is
concerned, she's lost.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.930
Mr. Otonashi, again?

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.420
She's going for
the umbrella gambit.

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:10.320
What does she see
in that old loser?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:11.950
Beats me.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.100
Mr. Otonashi?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:52.570
Come underneath.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:54.920
Okay.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.040
You're from
homeroom 3, right?

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.550
Yes. Kyoko Chigusa.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.060
--Miss Chigusa?
--Yes?

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.920
That must be cold.
You'll catch your death.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.320
That was an unusual
thing to try.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.120
I thought it
was brilliant.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.770
Your high school teacher--

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.390
Well, actually he was
temporarily assigned.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.200
Still, it's so romantic to
marry your first love.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:36.950
Oh, yeah!

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:44.000
I'd love to see
Your high school picture albums.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.020
M-My pictures?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:51.850
Sure. I'm feeling a little
nostalgic myself right now.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.580
Just till
Godai comes home.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:57.930
Sure. Until
he comes home.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.420
I'll wait until the
rain lightens up.

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.670
Well, it's getting
kinda late--

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:41.170
I wonder what became of Godai.
He's usually home by now.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.830
It was fun
seelng your pictures.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.760
Come back
again, okay?

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:46.780
Okay.
Come back
again, okay?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.180
Okay.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:51.040
Goodbye!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:51.770
Goodbye.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:19.800
I was so young.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.250
The costume competition.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.040
Oh, Soichiro!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.560
Mr. and Mrs. Otonashi!!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:39.910
I'm home!

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.750
Godai, what HAVE
you been doing?

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.450
Kozue was waiting for
you all afternoon!

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.370
What? She came
over? Here?

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:57.500
Yes. You should call her.
She waited all day.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:02.390
Maybe she did, but--
But-

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.040
You know--
You see, I--

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.280
She and I aren't--
You got it wrong--

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:10.380
I-- I don't--
There's nothing--

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.680
What are you saying?
That's not the point.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.750
I don't need to call her. We
aren't...that way, after all.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:18.370
Godai, wait--

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.680
Honestly!
What is he thinking?

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.140
Manager!

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:26.260
Mrs. Ichinose.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.230
Come on in.
Come in.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:30.550
What's going on?

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.770
Hello, Kozue?
Yeah, it's me, Godai.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.040
I heard you came by.
What's up?

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:58.550
I see. We'll get
together tomorrow.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.830
School? I'll cut classes.
Naw, don't worry.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.650
Listen to him.
Ya jealous?

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:06.930
Oh, please.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.330
Yeah, see you then.

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:18.560
What a fool.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:21.880
I'm off!

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.300
Wait a sec, Godai.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.050
Give this umbrella
back to Kozue, please?

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.100
She left it behind.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:35.100
But l was
going to classes...

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.370
Going to CUT classes
and meet Kozue, right?

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.840
How did you
know that?

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.500
I'm the manager.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.470
She and I aren't--
You got it wrong--

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:50.830
Don't try to keep it such
a big secret. You'll disappoint Kozue.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:55.030
You'll ruin the image
of her first love!

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:56.550
What's that mean?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:58.940
Maybe I shouldn't say.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:02.690
What do you mean by
''image of her first love''?

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.040
You look just like
Kozue's first love.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:13.350
Oh, so I'm not
her first love.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:15.310
She said he
was wonderful.

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:18.860
She said that
he was wonderful.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:25.410
So you should try to act more
dignified, for Kozue's sake.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:27.760
S-Sure.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.250
Act more dignified
For Kozue's sake?

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.630
What do YOU
know about it?

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.380
You know better
than that!

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:41.470
What's going on? She used
to be jealous of Kozue!

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.550
So you heard about
my first love?

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:49.990
I'm sorry.
Are you mad?

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:50.550
Why?

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:53.990
Wouldn't you hate being cast
in the shadow of another guy?

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:56.370
It's not a problem.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:00.020
But I'd like you to
see me for who I am.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:01.730
I do!

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.690
Your manager is great.

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:07.980
Yesterday, she told me
all about her husband.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.270
What kind of... stuff?

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:15.740
Something that happened on
a rainy day. Her first love!

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.300
They were so in love!

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:29.600
Could someone as reserved
as Kyoko be so passionate?

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.900
The picture of true love!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:40.240
I think it's great when two
people in love can be together.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.040
Yeah.
But now he's dead.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:45.560
That's true.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.310
Please, Godai
don't die on me!.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.760
I just couldn't
bear it.

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:09.640
Y-You're such a kidder.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:36.990
Perhaps you call this sorrow.
It's more than I can bear.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.380
He's still there.
Soichiro--

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:44.160
Kyoko's a fool.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:46.810
Binding her self
to a dead man!

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:52.210
Damn! Why can't she
see that I'm right here!

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:02.340
Godai?

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:06.720
Come under.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:20.620
No thanks.
I want to be alone!

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:22.810
But--

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:26.890
Stop that!
You'll catch cold!

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:28.180
Leave me alone!

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:31.990
What's he
pouting about?

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:41.940
Damn! What do YOU
know about it?

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:44.380
You know better
than that!

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:47.020
But maybe someday...

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:49.230
Someday...

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.020
Oh, dear.

00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:19.440
I'm sorry.
Please let me under.

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:32.820
See? You caught cold.

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:51.000
Time flies.

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:54.240
This'll be my second Christmas
since I came to Maison Ikkoku.

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:57.210
Godai, it's a
gift from the heart.

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:01.910
Next: ''Kyoko's Gift!
What, You Mean It's For Me?'''

00:24:03.050 --> 00:24:04.540
I knitted it for
all I was worth.

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:06.410
But--
